title: Radek in Berlin
subtitle: Moscow's German expert arrives under a false name.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('m_radek'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('m_radek');
Q.lw_name = RG.pick(['a Polish timber merchant', 'an Austrian journalist', 'a Latvian professor of economics', 'a Swiss dealer in watches']);
!}

= Radek in Berlin

**Karl Radek** is in Berlin again, travelling as [+ lw_name +], which deceives nobody who has heard him laugh. He has taken a flat in the west of the city, and in a week he has seen half the Zentrale, two ministers' secretaries, a general's adjutant and the editor of a nationalist weekly.

He is brilliant, cynical and very well informed. He smokes a pipe, tells jokes in four languages and knows the German party better than most of its members. [? if ecci_radek >= 60 : He likes the Zentrale, and says so. ?][? if ecci_radek < 40 : He thinks the Zentrale is stumbling, and says that too, to anyone. ?]

He wants to sit in on the Zentrale's meetings. "As an observer, of course."

- @seat: Give him a seat at the table.
- @frontline: Ask his help for the united front.
- @factions: Let him bring the currents to one table.
- @distance: Keep him at arm's length.

@seat
subtitle: Moscow's voice inside the Zentrale. Radek is pleased; our independence suffers.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', 10);
RG.ecci('all', 2);
Q.independence -= 5;
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 3);
!}

Radek takes the chair at the end of the table and observes for a week. In the second week, he drafts the resolutions. Nobody can quite say when that started.

@frontline
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Radek knows the social democrats' leaders, and they know him. The Right's line.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids any deal with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('united_front');
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.uspd_relation += 3;
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 2, 5);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', -1, -4);
!}

Radek has lunch with a union leader and dinner with a deputy of the SPD, and comes back with a list of things they would be willing to do together, and a list of things they would say they would never do.

@factions
subtitle: A peacemaker from Moscow. The currents talk; the Zentrale's own people feel overruled.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity += 4;
RG.ecci('radek', 5);
Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 3;
Q.independence -= 2;
!}

Radek invites the leaders of every current to his flat and makes them all laugh, which no German has managed in a year. They leave with a compromise each of them thinks he won.

@distance
subtitle: The Zentrale runs its own meetings. Radek is offended, and will write to Moscow about it.
on-arrival: {!
RG.ecci('radek', -7);
Q.independence += 4;
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 4);
!}

Radek is welcome at any time, the Zentrale tells him, as a guest of the party. Its meetings are for its members. He smiles, and starts writing a letter.
